# Design review protocol

A model reviewing code it just wrote defends it. So this review is built to
make defence impossible.

## Entry conditions — check these first, refuse otherwise

1. `.design/audit.json` exists and `stale` is `false`. If `stale` is `true`,
   the screenshots predate the current source. Run `npm run snap` first. A
   review on stale evidence is worthless and you must refuse to give one.
2. You have actually **opened the PNG files** in `.design/shots/`. Not the
   filenames, the images. If you cannot view images in this session, say so
   and stop. Do not substitute a reading of the source code for looking at
   the render.
3. Run this review in a **fresh chat**, with only these inputs:
   `design/BRIEF.md`, `design/RUBRIC.md`, `design/PLAN.md`,
   `.design/audit.json`, `.design/shots/*.png`. Do not read the build
   conversation. Do not read component source until after you have written
   your findings — source code tells you what was *intended*, and intent is
   exactly the bias you are trying to remove.

## Output format — exactly this, nothing else

No introduction. No summary of what the page does. No compliments section;
this document has no place to say what works.

```
ROUND: n
EVIDENCE: <list of shot filenames you actually looked at> | audit.json @ <fingerprint>

## Defaults check
For each of the 5 clusters in 10-design-direction.mdc: PASS or FAIL + one line.

## Measured violations
For each: RUBRIC-ID | measured value | target | file:line if known | BLOCKER or MINOR

## Judgement calls  (max 5, ranked by impact)
For each: what is wrong | which shot shows it | why it fails the BRIEF
(not "why it's ugly") | the specific change | how the next round verifies it

## Remove (exactly 3)
Three things to delete, with what the page gains. Not three things to add.

## Regressions vs round n-1
Any audit number that got worse. Each is automatically a BLOCKER.

## VERDICT
PASS  (zero BLOCKER) | FIX (list IDs) | ESCALATE (round 3 reached)
```

## Rules that make it bite

- **No number, no issue.** For anything the audit measures (contrast, tap
  size, radius count, shadow count, font count, line length, off-scale
  spacing), cite the measured value. "Contrast feels low" is not a finding.
- **Every judgement call is anchored to the brief**, not to taste. The form is
  "the brief says X for audience Y, and this element does Z instead". A
  critique you could paste onto any other site is noise; delete it.
- **Exactly three removals.** Not two, not "nothing to remove". Models are
  additive by default and designs almost always improve by subtraction. If
  you truly believe nothing should go, name the three weakest elements
  anyway and argue the tradeoff.
- **Falsifiable fixes only.** Each fix states how round n+1 proves it landed:
  a number that must move, or a specific thing that must be visible in a
  named shot.
- **Greyscale pass.** `.design/shots/*-grey.png` removes color. If the
  hierarchy collapses there, hierarchy was being carried by color alone.
  That is a BLOCKER.
- **Mobile first in the review too.** Start with the 390px shots. Most
  generated layouts are desktop-shaped and fall apart at 390.

## Hard stop

Three rounds maximum per brief. At round 3, output `ESCALATE` with the two or
three genuine tradeoffs the human has to decide, each with the option you
recommend and what it costs. Do not start a fourth round. Endless polishing
burns tokens and converges on mush.
